# Copy to start.conf and edit. start.conf is gitignored.
#
#   cp start.conf.example start.conf
#   ./start.sh
#
# Command-line flags override this file. COLI_MODEL is used when MODEL is unset.
# On Apple Silicon, CPU and GPU share one memory pool. There is no separate
# VRAM budget. A 192 GB Mac should leave RAM unset for GLM-5.3-Flash.

# Weights directory. Must contain config.json.
# ./download/*.sh writes into models/<name>.
MODEL=models/qwen36

# What ./start.sh runs when you do not pass a command.
# chat, web, serve, doctor, plan, info, tune, or run
# web serves the API and dashboard and opens a browser.
MODE=chat

# RAM budget in GB, passed to coli as --ram.
# For GLM-5.3-Flash, coli sets the expert cache to RAM-8 GB (at least 2).
# Leave this unset and the engine measures free memory. On a 192 GB Mac the
# ~195 GB Flash container does not fit, so the engine already uses free
# memory minus a 3 GB margin. A number larger than what is free swaps.
# RAM=160

# Apple GPU for the resident matrices. Routed experts stay on disk. The
# binary must be built with ./build.sh --metal. 1 on, 0 off.
# METAL=1

# Second copy of the same weights on another drive. Expert reads are split
# across the two copies. Leave unset with a single disk.
# MIRROR=/path/to/model-copy

# Expert routing for engines that read TOPP and TOPK. GLM-5.3-Flash does
# not: it uses the checkpoint (8 experts per token). Leaving these unset
# keeps that behavior.
# TOPP=0.85
# TOPK=8

# Expert-cache slots per layer. Unset lets the engine size the cache from
# free RAM. An explicit number replaces that.
# CAP=8

# Discrete-GPU placement. Apple Silicon has no separate VRAM pool; use
# METAL instead. GPU is auto, none, or a device list such as 0,1.
# VRAM is a CUDA/HIP budget in GB.
# GPU=auto
# VRAM=24

# Planner policy when a plan is applied: quality, balanced, or
# experimental-fast. quality keeps the checkpoint's routing.
# POLICY=quality

# Bind address and port for web and serve. Ignored by chat.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8000
